#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Faction, technique catalog, and Part 2 pages. No em-dashes."""
from page_lib import page, crumb, hero

page(
    "factions/hishaku.html",
    "The Hishaku",
    "The ten criminal sorcerers who murdered Kunishige Rokuhira and stole six Enchanted Blades.",
    crumb(("Factions", "index.html"), "Hishaku")
    + hero("Ten sorcerers · flame tattoos", "The Hishaku", "毘灼", "They killed the smith, stole six blades, and spent three years trying to open contracts by killing the people still tied to them.")
    + """
    <article class="article">
      <p>The Hishaku are ten elite criminal sorcerers. Flame-emblem tattoos. A shared fire-gate. They formed about four years before the main story with one plan for Shinuchi. Three years before the present, they raided the Rokuhira house, murdered <a href="../characters/kunishige.html">Kunishige</a>, and stole the six wartime Enchanted Blades. <a href="../blades/enten.html">Enten</a> stayed with the son. In the same campaign they killed <a href="../characters/ibuki.html">Ibuki Misaka</a> so Cloud Gouger’s Lifelong Contract would open. They are not a gang that happened to find swords. They are a method: open the knot, spend the steel, change the country.</p>
      <p>They are allied with Korogumi yakuza and, fatally, with at least one Kamunabi head. <a href="../characters/kasen.html">Kasen</a> leaked the smith’s address because he thought Enchanted Blades were a path to order. The Hishaku were the path he hired. Recaps that call <a href="../characters/sojo.html">Sojo</a> Hishaku cannot explain <a href="../characters/yura.html">Yura</a>. Sojo is a customer. They handed him Cloud Gouger in early October. He used it to chase Char and the idea that he could fake Kunishige’s eyes. They listed Magatsumi at the 208th Rakuzaichi after Yura cracked the seal and left the ropes. They signed a private contract with <a href="../characters/samura.html">Samura</a>. They are the men who sold a sword, auctioned a masterpiece, and tried to kidnap a daughter so a father would flinch.</p>
      <p>Eight of the ten are named on this site. This archive will not invent the other two. The named eight are enough to see the labor split: a mind, a swordsman who wants a real fight, a child who killed at three, a tracker, an ice user, a lion-dancer who eats corpses, a seventeen-year-old regenerator in a barrier, and a man courting a blade that will not sign him.</p>

      <h2>The method</h2>
      <p>Lifelong Contracts bind a blade to one nervous system. Kill the bearer, the contract opens, someone else can sign. Magatsumi’s contract is the master key: if Akemura dies, the other five wartime bearers die with him. Destroy Magatsumi and the knot comes apart. For three years the Hishaku hit Sanso fortresses trying to open the wartime five that were still alive. Samura’s side deal looked like a shortcut: he would eliminate bearers, return blades, kill the Sword Master, then die with the Hishaku. He was lying about the dying. Suzaku can kill a contract and keep the man. Yura anticipated betrayal anyway and attacked Kamunabi headquarters while other members went after Iori.</p>
      <p>The shared fire-gate is logistics. Toto uses it as a habit, pulling comrades out of fatal rooms. The tattoos are the uniform. The plan for Shinuchi mutated. Yura wanted the Sword Master dead so he could wield the masterpiece. Then he spoke to Akemura in the cell, found him sane, and offered a body. The ten did not vote on that. The mind of the set changed the math, and Part 1 ended with the basement wearing the leader.</p>

      <h2>The named ten (eight printed)</h2>
      <h3>Yura 幽</h3>
      <p>Leader. Calm enough to bet his life on a coin, sure God is on his side. He ordered the raid, sold Cloud Gouger, cracked Magatsumi’s seal, listed it at the Rakuzaichi, and visited Samura at home to write a contract. He had a wife; she died. He wanted Akemura dead, then wanted Akemura as a colleague. Gravely wounded by Chihiro, he gave the body. Full file: <a href="../characters/yura.html">Yura</a>.</p>
      <h3>Hokuto 北兜</h3>
      <p>Swordsman in samurai clothes. Armored puppet that resembles himself; piece control for defense. Present at Kunishige’s murder. Assassin of Ibuki. Disappointed that the wartime equal of Samura had already retired. Wants deadly battles, especially with Uruha. Volume 10 jacket with Natsuki, Uruha, and Yura. Full file: <a href="../characters/hokuto.html">Hokuto</a>.</p>
      <h3>Hiruhiko 昼彦</h3>
      <p>Eighteen. Killed an assailant at age three. Blood Crane (Chizuru): razor origami, lifting Datenseki fragments. Assigned to kill Uruha, met Chihiro on the train, treated him as a peer-shaped friend. Contracted Kumeyuri after Samura’s false death, two-handed, Play as demolition. Lost the blade to Samura at the hotel. Full file: <a href="../characters/hiruhiko.html">Hiruhiko</a>.</p>
      <h3>Kuguri 久々李</h3>
      <p>Twilight Wave (Hagure): banks kinetic energy and heat, spends it later. Carries an Enchanted Blade without a contract; calls it unrequited love. Sent with Toto to take Iori. Abandoned the kidnapping when Chihiro’s fake Iai got serious. Full file: <a href="../characters/kuguri.html">Kuguri</a>.</p>
      <h3>Toto 斗斗</h3>
      <p>Blood tracking and extraction. Locates Iori from a sample taken off Samura at Senkutsuji. At the Kyoto Bloodshed Hotel she reads Sengoku’s severed head the same way. Prefers the fire-gate to the cut. The ten’s extraction specialist. Not given a solo encyclopedia page yet; she lives here and on the hotel chapters (67–74).</p>
      <h3>Uran 右嵐</h3>
      <p>Ice. Breath that freezes and restrains. Present at Kunishige’s murder with Hokuto and the third raider. Named; not yet given a room of her own on this site. The raid was three sorcerers. She is one of the three.</p>
      <h3>Bingo 瓶伍</h3>
      <p>Mako (Demon Bite): lion-dancer heads, “lucky charms,” mouths that hit hard. Destroying them stacks an invisible weight on whoever did the destroying. He can turn his own head into a charm and eat corpses to fuel the art, then gets sleepy. HQ infiltration muscle. Named with the ten; the pages have not given him a domestic scene.</p>
      <h3>Yukisada 幸禎</h3>
      <p>Seventeen. Yura calls him the strongest fighter among the Hishaku. Regeneration that survives decapitation. Became a Vessel so he could manipulate Kamunabi headquarters’ barrier from inside, splitting control with the Kamunabi’s own vessel and shutting the building against relief. Hakuri, Kiri, and Hagiwara cannot kill him cleanly. The solution is Storehouse: remove the Kamunabi vessel from the split rather than win a regeneration duel. Yukisada is why Azami cannot simply call Shiba until the field is restored. Volume 11, <em>Heroes</em>, is his lock on the cell.</p>

      <h2>What they are not</h2>
      <p>They are not the Kamunabi. Kasen used them; they used Kasen. They are not the Sazanami. Kyora auctioned their listing and died touching it. They are not Sojo’s gang. Madoka, the Daruma sorcerer, worked for the customer and died for talking. They are not the Mikaboshi. The old sorcerer kings are Part 2’s island problem. The Hishaku are a present-tense conspiracy that stole a war’s leftovers and then, at the last hour, handed the leftovers back to the man who had already spent 200,000 civilians.</p>
      <p>After Yura’s body is no longer Yura’s, the ten do not automatically become Akemura’s squad. Possession is not a merger. This page will not invent a new org chart the magazine has not printed. What is printed: flame tattoos, fire-gate, eight names, two still unlabeled, a raid, a sale, an auction listing, a hotel kidnapping, a headquarters attack, a cell conversation, a body offered. The <a href="index.html">factions index</a> places them next to Kamunabi and Sazanami. The <a href="../world/techniques.html">technique catalog</a> places their arts next to the blades they stole.</p>
      <p class="related"><a href="kamunabi.html">Kamunabi</a><a href="../characters/yura.html">Yura</a><a href="../characters/hokuto.html">Hokuto</a><a href="../characters/kuguri.html">Kuguri</a><a href="../arcs/sword-bearer.html">Sword Bearer Assassination</a></p>
    </article>
    """,
)

page(
    "factions/kamunabi.html",
    "The Kamunabi",
    "State sorcerers: leadership, Hiyuki, Sanso fortresses, the leak, and the basement they called a victory.",
    crumb(("Factions", "index.html"), "Kamunabi")
    + hero("State sorcerers", "The Kamunabi", "神奈備", "Rebuilt from an army so Japan could have a bureau. They sealed a masterpiece, hid a smith, leaked the address, and still want the blades under a stamp.")
    + """
    <article class="article">
      <p>The Kamunabi are a government-backed agency of sorcerers. Civilian sorcerers handle small jobs. The Kamunabi exist because some jobs are national. Their origin is the Sorcery Bureau, then the Counter-Sorcery Army, then a bureau again: military hierarchy abandoned so the state could counter sorcerers from Shokoku without looking like a standing army forever. The current priority is securing Enchanted Blades. For three years they have been locked in a fight with the <a href="hishaku.html">Hishaku</a>, who have the steel and cannot fully use it while the bearers live. The Kamunabi’s answer was Sanso fortresses. The Hishaku’s answer was killing bearers. A director’s answer was leaking <a href="../characters/kunishige.html">Kunishige</a> so the blades might, in his fantasy, return to the state as tools of order.</p>
      <p>They are not a monolith. Azami helped hide the smith and hates the ten. Kudo dies for Hakuri. Ichiki trained Shiba and Azami. Yatsuru sealed Shinuchi with Kasen. Izaru distrusts Chihiro and talks as if Kunishige stole national property. <a href="../characters/kasen.html">Kasen</a> is the leak. <a href="../characters/hiyuki.html">Hiyuki</a> is the pointed end. <a href="../characters/tafuku.html">Tafuku</a> is the referee. The Anti-Cloud Gouger Special Forces were six people built to solve one stolen sword; four of them die in the first book. This page is the org chart the <a href="index.html">factions index</a> could not hold.</p>

      <h2>Leadership</h2>
      <p><strong>Kasen</strong> (嘉仙), director. Long beard. Barriers and sealing. Sealed Shinuchi with Ichiki and Yatsuru after the war. Laments that major sorcery clans will not respect a bureau. Believes Enchanted Blades can create order. Conspired with the Hishaku and leaked Kunishige’s location. Full file: <a href="../characters/kasen.html">Kasen</a>.</p>
      <p><strong>Ichiki</strong> (壱鬼). Elderly, small, learned arts and physical combat. Trained Shiba and Azami during the war. Helped seal Shinuchi and hide Kunishige. One of the White Robes.</p>
      <p><strong>Yatsuru</strong> (夜弦). Sole woman among the named leaders. Barrier and sealing, same desk as Kasen and Ichiki. Instrumental in the Shinuchi seal. When Yukisada splits the HQ barrier, her life’s work is the thing being stolen from inside.</p>
      <p><strong>Soshiro Azami</strong> (薊 奏士郎). Strongest of the heads. Coin (Koin): family clinic art adapted into combat, which earned his father’s ire. Helped hide Kunishige. Informant to Chihiro. Executioner manners. Kills the Shigyu brothers when they punch into Level 1. Full file: <a href="../characters/azami.html">Azami</a>.</p>
      <p><strong>Izaru</strong> (亥猿). Mutton chops. Rosary-like bead chains to restrict a target. Criticized colleagues for hiding Kunishige, talked as if the smith stole the blades, distrusts Chihiro. The leadership table’s prosecutor.</p>
      <p><strong>Kudo</strong> (区堂). Gas-mask apparatus, one eye closed. Warrior’s Path (Shitō): send a body in a direction, through walls and floors. Supporter of Kunishige. Dies protecting Hakuri during the HQ assault. The bureau’s best argument that not everyone in the building was Kasen.</p>

      <h2>Operations</h2>
      <p><strong>Hiyuki Kagari</strong> and <strong>Tafuku Mihara</strong> are the celebrity pair: Flame Bone of the Starving versus a duel domain. Assigned to problems the organization cannot file. They start as Chihiro’s enemies at the Rakuzaichi and become the reason the auction actually ends. Files: <a href="../characters/hiyuki.html">Hiyuki</a>, <a href="../characters/tafuku.html">Tafuku</a>. Essay: <a href="../analysis/flame-bone.html">Flame Bone</a>.</p>
      <p><strong>Natsuki Misaka</strong>, squadron leader, Lightning Menace, Ibuki’s brother, Volume 10 jacket. <strong>Kiri Shirakai</strong>, squadron leader, two-meter odachi, granddaughter of Iai’s founder. Files: <a href="../characters/natsuki.html">Natsuki</a>, <a href="../characters/kiri.html">Kiri</a>.</p>
      <p><strong>Anti-Cloud Gouger Special Forces</strong>: Ikuto Hagiwara (Jikai, magnetism; loses both legs; later hallucinates Kugara), Hajime Kugara (iron body; dies; the hallucination’s face), Kazane Machi (Demon Monster, Kaichi, the unused secret weapon; loses an arm), Shiyumi Harima (Gansui, stone), Kiyohiko Uzuki (binding), Makoto Kasahara (enlarged hands). Four dead at Sojo’s compound. The two survivors are still in the HQ chapters. Hagiwara’s chapter title in the long book is “Ikuto Hagiwara, Worthless Commander.” The book is cruel about institutions that spend specialists and then name the leftover.</p>
      <p><strong>Kokugoku Steam Squad</strong>, including Fushimi (Smoke Axe), guard Uruha’s Sanso. They beat Datenseki-powered hired troops, then die to Hiruhiko. <strong>Masumi</strong> (Ro, Moku, Sumi) serve Samura until he frees them, then protect Iori in Operation: Easy Does It. Ro looks like a child, copies Samura’s sunglasses and candy cigarettes, recovers Kumeyuri after the hotel. Sumi draws transportation mandalas and rides a motorcycle away from Kuguri. Moku feeds Chihiro when the boy starts eating himself.</p>
      <p><strong>Sanso</strong> fortresses are where surviving wartime bearers were locked after the raid. Kokugoku Hot Spring. Senkutsuji Temple. The next book of Part 1 starts when one is attacked. Subaru Urita is relocated when the pattern becomes obvious. See <a href="../characters/subaru.html">Subaru</a> and <a href="../world/locations.html">locations</a>.</p>

      <h2>Chihiro’s deal</h2>
      <p>After the Rakuzaichi, Chihiro hands Magatsumi to the Kamunabi and keeps Enten by joining them. Hakuri’s Storehouse is the reason the table listens: bearers can be un-armed and re-armed without a siege. The deal assumes a bureau that wants blades sealed. Kasen’s faction wanted them used. Those two bureaus share a building until Yura walks to the cell. Then Akemura takes the building. Part 1’s last political fact is that the state which covered up Malediction has been possessed by Malediction’s author. Part 2 does not stay to run the press conference. It goes to Irishima, where the bureau is still a Sorcery Bureau and the blades are still a proposal.</p>
      <p>Read officially on VIZ / MANGA Plus. For the ten who raided the house, see <a href="hishaku.html">Hishaku</a>. For the leak as a person, see <a href="../characters/kasen.html">Kasen</a>. For the myth, see the <a href="../analysis/malediction.html">Malediction essay</a>.</p>
      <p class="related"><a href="hishaku.html">Hishaku</a><a href="../characters/hiyuki.html">Hiyuki</a><a href="../characters/kasen.html">Kasen</a><a href="../characters/azami.html">Azami</a><a href="../world/contracts.html">Lifelong Contracts</a></p>
    </article>
    """,
)

page(
    "world/techniques.html",
    "Technique catalog",
    "Named Enchanted Blade techniques and major innate arts in Kagurabachi, listed without invented titles.",
    crumb(("World", "index.html"), "Techniques")
    + hero("Honryō and the kit", "Technique catalog", "技", "Five blades have printed technique lists. Two wartime swords still do not. Innate arts sit beside them so the book’s other weapons have a desk.")
    + """
    <article class="article">
      <p>An Enchanted Blade overfills. Spirit energy leaves the body as a shape that can be steered, seen through, and charged back into the steel so the bearer can spend techniques empty-handed. Most blades have three named techniques. Magatsumi refuses the three-count. <strong>True Realm</strong> (Honryō) is not a transformation gauge. It is the brief, meant: the wielder’s intent locking with the steel until the kit grows an extension. <strong>Dark power</strong> (Kuroi chikara) is what happens when that lock happens at the edge of death, or when the blade itself is dying. The color goes black. The output jumps. Mei: Shred. Suzaku’s black flames. Magatsumi’s ordinary darkness, because Magatsumi eats vitality as a diet.</p>
      <p>Unofficial names the fandom uses are marked with an asterisk where the pages themselves did not print a title. This catalog will not invent the two missing wartime blades. Full blade files: <a href="../blades/index.html">Enchanted Blades</a>. Contracts: <a href="contracts.html">Lifelong Contracts</a>. The essay: <a href="../analysis/true-realm.html">True Realm</a>.</p>

      <h2>Enten 淵天</h2>
      <p>Bearer: <a href="../characters/chihiro.html">Chihiro Rokuhira</a>. Seventh, post-war, goldfish and water. Made to end the other six, especially Magatsumi. True Realm: Magatsumi’s death.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Kuro 涅</strong>: black goldfish paints arm and edge; flying slash sized to the fish called.</li>
        <li><strong>Kuro: Shred 涅千</strong>: many small black fish, many small cuts, more spirit, less strain on the body. The fish can be moved as scouts and tools.</li>
        <li><strong>Aka 猩</strong>: red goldfish drinks an attack; speaking Aka plus the absorbed name spends it back for a short window.</li>
        <li><strong>Nishiki 錦</strong>: tricolor cloak of dense spirit. Speed, power, and resistance to other Enchanted Blade ailments (Spider, vitality-drain). The design brief, not a fashion layer.</li>
        <li><strong>Nishiki: Support*</strong>: wounded form. Supports movement instead of amplifying it. Less strain, still faster than an empty coat.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><span class="spoiler">Magatsumi bisects Enten at the end of Part 1. Black Suzaku stalls disintegration. Chihiro keeps the pieces and writes notes toward a new Enten.</span></p>

      <h2>Cloud Gouger 刳雲</h2>
      <p>Bearers: <a href="../characters/ibuki.html">Ibuki Misaka</a> → <a href="../characters/sojo.html">Sojo</a> → Chihiro (dying contract). Clouds and cloud-dragons. Bisected by Enten. Residual charges spent at the Rakuzaichi, then gone.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Mei 鳴</strong>: lightning bolt. Can charge; a heavy charge disables Mei for about 10–20 seconds until the bearer understands the sword better.</li>
        <li><strong>Cloaked Mei*</strong>: wear the lightning instead of throwing it. Sojo finds this first. Speed like a bolt.</li>
        <li><strong>Mei: Shred 鳴千</strong>: Chihiro, blade dying, black lightning. Dark power. Faster and meaner than white cloak.</li>
        <li><strong>Yui 結</strong>: ice, instant cages and constructs, amount variable with the point of the blade.</li>
        <li><strong>Kou 降</strong>: water or mist. Exists to make Mei a wire and Yui a larger freeze.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Sojo’s True Realm is slaughter, because that was his brief. Chihiro’s last Cloud Gouger is a partner he wants to die well. Same steel. Different lock.</p>

      <h2>Magatsumi 勾罪 (Shinuchi 真打)</h2>
      <p>Bearer: <a href="../characters/akemura.html">Akemura Soga</a>. Proxies: Kyora, then Yura, by overwriting, not by contract. Flowers, black weep, insects. No three-count. Master key of the wartime knot. Bypass: anyone who holds the sheathed blade starts becoming Akemura.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Spider 蛛</strong>: cobweb and eyes. Caught entities cannot move.</li>
        <li><strong>Dragonfly 蜻</strong>: wing shapes, directional blast. Hiyuki can mitigate with Flame Bone; blades can block.</li>
        <li><strong>Centipede 蜈</strong>: omnidirectional blast from circular structures. Weakest directly behind the wielder.</li>
        <li><strong>Butterfly 蝶</strong>: amplified slash through space. A building, then the buildings behind it.</li>
        <li><strong>Bee 蜂</strong>: rings, piercing blast widest at the origin and narrowest at the point.</li>
        <li><strong>Malediction 蠱 (Kodoku)</strong>: extension. True Realm as policy. Vitality drain at national scale, flowers, bloodlust as a targeting reticle. About 200,000 civilians after the treaty. Essay: <a href="../analysis/malediction.html">Malediction</a>.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Yura spends Magatsumi at range through spirit left in the blade, then offers the body. The insect kit is the war. The possession path is the unique clause. After chapter 119, explainers argue Magatsumi copies Ariu Mikaboshi’s insect sorcery. The archive files that as a camp next to the printed list, not as a caption on the steel.</p>

      <h2>Kumeyuri 酌揺</h2>
      <p>Fifth forged. Bearers: <a href="../characters/uruha.html">Uruha</a> → <a href="../characters/hiruhiko.html">Hiruhiko</a> → recovered by Ro of the Masumi. Faceless oiran. Hallucination and play. Natsuki was a candidate; Uruha was chosen.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Banquet 宴</strong>: intoxicating hallucinations. Reinforced ears mitigate. Fatal wounds can snap it.</li>
        <li><strong>Play 遊</strong>: manipulate nearby objects. Fluency scales with respect for the objects.</li>
        <li><strong>Destructive Play*</strong>: Hiruhiko’s extension. He does not respect objects. The upper Kyoto Bloodshed Hotel comes apart.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Uruha’s Crimson Recital (Koen) is not a blade technique. It is the innate art that comes back when Samura cuts the contract and keeps the man. Physical boost. The banquet sword is the job. The recital is the person.</p>

      <h2>Tobimune 飛宗</h2>
      <p>Support blade. Bearers: <a href="../characters/samura.html">Samura</a> → <span class="spoiler">Iori</span>. Black feathers, wings, flight. Owl at national scale. Chihiro notes it was forged for support.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Crow 鴉</strong>: swap places with a feather. A faint spirit trace lands on the chosen feather first.</li>
        <li><strong>External Crow*</strong>: move entities other than Samura and the blade.</li>
        <li><strong>Owl 梟</strong>: two giant owl eyes. Detection range versus precision tradeoff. Nationwide, only huge spirit sources ping.</li>
        <li><strong>Suzaku 雀</strong>: flames that heal the bearer, burn others, and can coat the blade. After the war Samura advanced this into resurrection: slash with Suzaku, the contract dies, the person walks.</li>
        <li><strong>External Suzaku*</strong>: heal others and restore ruined objects, including Tobimune itself.</li>
        <li><strong>Suzaku: Black Flames*</strong>: dark power. Samura spends his life. Black fire nullifies Magatsumi’s wide drain long enough for Chihiro to leave. Then Samura dies.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Unnamed wartime two</h2>
      <p>Two Enchanted Blades still have no printed names. <a href="../characters/subaru.html">Subaru Urita</a> is a surviving bearer; one war-ensemble portrait is still unlabeled. <a href="../characters/ibuki.html">Ibuki</a> is dead and his sword is Cloud Gouger, which is named. Do not assign Subaru a fish, a weather, or an insect. When Jump captions the steel, this catalog grows two headers.</p>

      <h2>Major innate arts (not blades)</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Shiba’s teleport</strong>: extraction, infiltration, civilian evacuation. Famous as a teenager. Not a bearer.</li>
        <li><strong>Azami’s Coin (Koin)</strong>: clinic stimulant rewritten as an executioner’s projectile.</li>
        <li><strong>Hakuri’s Isou and Storehouse</strong>: burial-force plus subspace. Dual inheritance, historically almost unique in the Sazanami.</li>
        <li><strong>Hiyuki’s Flame Bone</strong>: hereditary skeleton, licensed by the bureau, stood next to Enchanted Blades in the text. <a href="../analysis/flame-bone.html">Essay</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Tafuku’s duel domain</strong>: two people, one match, then the street returns. <a href="../characters/tafuku.html">Tafuku</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Natsuki’s Lightning Menace (Raiku)</strong>: voltage in the body, not Mei. <a href="../characters/natsuki.html">Natsuki</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Hokuto’s armored puppet</strong>: self-resembling armor, piece control. <a href="../characters/hokuto.html">Hokuto</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Kuguri’s Twilight Wave (Hagure)</strong>: bank motion and heat, spend later. <a href="../characters/kuguri.html">Kuguri</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Hiruhiko’s Blood Crane (Chizuru)</strong>: origami that cuts and lifts. Goes quiet when Kumeyuri is signed.</li>
        <li><strong>Toto’s blood tracking</strong>: locate and read through blood. Fire-gate as a habit.</li>
        <li><strong>Yukisada’s regeneration</strong>: survives decapitation; Vessel for the HQ barrier.</li>
        <li><strong>Bingo’s Mako</strong>: lion-dancer heads; stacked weight on destroyers; corpse-eating, then sleep.</li>
        <li><strong>Uran’s ice</strong>: freeze and restrain, including breath. Raid participant.</li>
        <li><strong>Char’s Kyonagi regeneration</strong>: close her own wounds and other people’s. Sojo’s stabilizer hunt.</li>
        <li><strong>Chiaki’s foresight</strong>: Princess Soga, inherited proof of Izanami. <a href="../characters/chiaki.html">Chiaki</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Hiroto Soga’s Kurotsuchi</strong>: directional gravity. Killed on Irishima by Ariu Mikaboshi.</li>
        <li><strong>Ariu Mikaboshi’s Sumika</strong>: insect constructs, poisoned air, Datenseki-hardened body. The camp that Magatsumi copies him.</li>
        <li><strong>Kudo’s Warrior’s Path</strong>: send a body through architecture. He spends it on Hakuri.</li>
        <li><strong>Izaru’s bead chains</strong>: restrict. Leadership table’s prosecutor kit.</li>
        <li><strong>Hagiwara’s Jikai</strong>: magnetism. Legs gone. Still in the HQ math.</li>
        <li><strong>Subaru’s duplication</strong>: several Subarus. A contract-opening assassination’s nightmare.</li>
        <li><strong>Mashiro’s Akuu</strong>: air pressure, hands-free weapons. Dies on Irishima. Part 2 still has him alive in the talks.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Iai White Purity is a school, not an innate art. Eyes closed, speed as a religion. See <a href="iai.html">Iai</a>. Datenseki that is not a blade still overfills and pops the user unless Kunishige’s eyes (or a fake, which kills Tenri and Sojo) intervene. See <a href="datenseki.html">Datenseki</a>.</p>
      <p class="related"><a href="../blades/index.html">Blades</a><a href="sorcery.html">Sorcery</a><a href="../analysis/true-realm.html">True Realm essay</a><a href="glossary.html">Glossary</a></p>
    </article>
    """,
)

page(
    "manga/part-2.html",
    "Part 2: the forge",
    "Kagurabachi Part 2 from Princess through Ironworks: Irishima, Chiaki, smelting, and chapter 129.",
    crumb(("Manga Guide", "index.html"), "Part 2")
    + hero("Ch. 116–129 · unfinished", "Part 2: the forge", "第二部", "The present tense ends on Swordsmith. The war book opens on a princess, four talks, fire, and a smith who has not yet looked at the stone that will make his friend a god.")
    + """
    <article class="article">
      <figure class="shot">
        <img src="../assets/panels/ch113.png" alt="Chapter 113 color page, the island">
        <figcaption>Chapter 113: the island-rising page. Part 2 is that clock, finally counted in workshop hours. Full chapter: VIZ / MANGA Plus.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <p>Part 1 runs chapters 1 through 115. “Swordsmith” (刀匠) closes the present tense: Enten in pieces, Samura dead, Akemura loose in the Kamunabi, Chihiro thinking like a smith again. Part 2 opens on chapter 116, “Princess” (姫), and does not stay for the press conference. It goes to Irishima. The Seitei War is not a clip show. It is the talks, the ore, the woman who can see, and the fire that turns a mineral into six national sins and, later, a seventh apology. This page is the magazine desk for that book. The <a href="../arcs/seitei-war.html">arc entry</a> is the political frame. The <a href="chapters.html">chapter index</a> is the title list. After chapter 126 the serial took an announced rest; 127–129 are the smelting continuing. Volume 12 (4 September 2026, ISBN 978-4-08-885177-8) is expected to close Part 1’s last corridor and open this one on paper.</p>

      <h2>How the split works</h2>
      <p>The title language already told you the present was a prologue. Early chapters are objects and meals. The long book names people, then puts quotation marks on the press’s words: “Strongest,” “Sword Master,” “Heroes.” Part 2 opens on a rank and a place. Princess. The Irishima Talks, four times, then END. Chiaki. Powerless. Smelting. Fire. Smelting again. Ironworks. The book is in the room where the sins are still a proposal. Chihiro has not been born. Enten does not exist. Shiba is still a Soga guardian. Mashiro is still alive. Kunishige is still a picky weapons dealer who barely eats because he will not sell to people he cannot stand.</p>
      <p>Do not Skypeia the flashback. The useful YouTube caution is twenty to forty chapters, not a clip show. The printed run through 129 is still the talks and the first steel. When a video outruns the magazine, it belongs on the <a href="../media/index.html">theory desk</a>, not in this entry.</p>

      <h2>The talks (116–122)</h2>
      <p><strong>116 Princess.</strong> Chiaki Soga, Chihiro’s mother, holder of the Princess Soga title, foresight as inherited proof of Izanami. She and her younger brother Akemura were elevated from a lower branch when the main-line prophetess died without children. The government listens to her because the clan has been the mainland’s warning system for a thousand years. The island in the sea is the old Mikaboshi kings coming back for Datenseki. The talks are what you do when a princess can see a war and a bureau still wants a treaty.</p>
      <p><strong>117–121 The Irishima Talks</strong> (杁島会談), four numbered pieces and “END.” Japan wants the vein. The Mikaboshi want Irishima and a foothold. Ariu, crown prince, insect sorcery (Sumika), poisoned air, a body that can live with Datenseki. Hiroto and Yoshinojo Soga will die on that island; they are not dead yet in these chapters. Hasumi runs a secret Datenseki lab and is not yet sure Kunishige is the answer. Shiba already is sure. Mashiro, Shiba’s partner, opposes taking stolen ore to a picky smith and will die later anyway. Joji is the annoyed senior at the lab. The negotiation is the war before the blades: what a state will prefer to a living island.</p>
      <p><strong>122 Start</strong> (始動). The talks end. The process begins. English explainers after 118 and 122 floated paternity rumors; face, eye, and the absence of insect sorcery still point at the smith as Chihiro’s father. This archive does not host the rumor as fact. Kunishige’s eyes are the only printed way to stabilize Datenseki. That is the plot, not a spoiler channel.</p>

      <h2>Chiaki, powerless, fire (123–126)</h2>
      <p><strong>123 Chiaki.</strong> The princess as a person, not only a title. She is romantically tied to Kunishige. Akemura is her younger brother, not yet the Sword Master, still the friend a smith can trust. Giyu Soga, Hiroto’s ambitious younger brother, is the kind of heir who might accept Mikaboshi demands that include handing Chiaki over. The clan is not a single will. Foresight is a warrant. It is also a hostage tag.</p>
      <p><strong>124 Powerless</strong> (無力). The word is the bureau’s Datenseki research, the army’s first year, and Kunishige’s civilian smallness before anyone asks him to look at the stone. Hokazono talked to a real swordsmith so the workshop pages would not be cosplay. Powerless is the last honest title before the fire starts lying that a man is a weapon.</p>
      <p><strong>125 Smelting</strong> (製鉄) and <strong>126 Fire</strong> (火). The archive’s smithing manual begins. About 250 kilograms of Datenseki are known in the present; here the vein is still a political object. Unstable, it pops the user. Kunishige’s eyes watch detail until the mineral can be a blade instead of a crater. The goldfish bowl is not on the table yet. The household that will become Enten’s language is still in the future. This is the kiln that will make Magatsumi possible, which will make Malediction possible, which will make Enten necessary. Chapter 126 is why the serial then took a month. Fire is not a metaphor in a smith’s shop.</p>

      <h2>The rest of the smelting (127–129)</h2>
      <p>The book returned from rest in August 2026. <strong>127 Smelting, Part 2</strong> (製鉄 弐) and <strong>128 Smelting, Part 3</strong> (製鉄 参) keep the process on the page. The first Enchanted Blade is not a montage. It is labor, failure, heat, and a pair of eyes that can see what the Bureau’s lab cannot. Subaru Urita, prolific smith and sushi chef, is the colleague who will help start this project; whether he is already in the room in these chapters is a caption this page will add when the magazine makes it cheap to source. Until then: Kunishige is the eyes. The ore is the problem. The war is the customer.</p>
      <p><strong>129 Ironworks</strong> (製鉄 肆), 23 August 2026. Kunishige at the edge of the process. Flashback inside the flashback: Chiaki has become Princess Soga, distance opens, Shiba tells him not to lose hope. The flames threaten to take the shop. Memories of the worst days arrive first. Then Chiaki arrives as the reason to keep the eyes open. He pushes further. The chapter ends with the fire beginning to settle, the first blade not yet confirmed as finished. Shiba’s willingness to risk himself for the smith is already the friendship that will later walk out of the Kamunabi when the smith hides. The princess is already the hope that Part 1’s son will inherit as a bowl of fish instead of a prophecy.</p>
      <p>The next chapter is expected to stay on the iron. This entry moves when 130 prints. Official reading: <a href="https://www.viz.com/shonenjump/chapters/kagurabachi">VIZ</a> and <a href="https://mangaplus.shueisha.co.jp/titles/100274">MANGA Plus</a>. We do not host chapters.</p>

      <h2>What Part 2 is for</h2>
      <p>To show the war the jackets called heroic before it had heroes. To show Akemura before Malediction as a brother a princess loves and a friend a smith trusts. To show Datenseki as work rather than a boss monster. To show Shiba before teleport-dad, Mashiro before a grave, Hasumi before resignation, the Mikaboshi before they are a theory about Magatsumi’s insects. Chihiro’s revenge was the engine of Part 1. Inheritance is the forge he actually gets. Part 2 is the forge before the inheritance, when the steel is still innocent and the people are not.</p>
      <p>Volume 11, <em>Heroes</em>, is snow and goldfish and the Sword Master standing up. Volume 12 is listed to carry “Karma” through “Swordsmith” and then the war book’s first signatures. English editions trail by about nine months. Jacket studies stay on the <a href="covers.html">cover page</a>. The present-tense aftermath (Akemura in the bureau, Iori with Tobimune, Chihiro with pieces) is paused, not cancelled. When Jump cuts back, this desk will say so.</p>
      <p class="related"><a href="../arcs/seitei-war.html">Seitei War arc</a><a href="../characters/chiaki.html">Chiaki</a><a href="../characters/kunishige.html">Kunishige</a><a href="chapters.html">Chapter index</a><a href="../world/datenseki.html">Datenseki</a></p>
    </article>
    """,
)

page(
    "analysis/irishima.html",
    "Irishima’s vein",
    "Why Kagurabachi’s war is a fight over a quarter-ton of rock, and why Part 2 has to smelt it in public.",
    crumb(("Essays", "index.html"), "Irishima’s vein")
    + hero("Essay · Part 2", "Irishima’s vein", "杁島", "The island is not a twist. It is the mineral the present has been swimming in since page one, finally shown as work.")
    + """
    <article class="article">
      <p>About 250 kilograms of Datenseki are known. One pair of eyes ever made it safe. The Seitei War is, at the mineral level, a fight over a vein that showed after an earthquake on Irishima and a nation that rose from the sea. Everything else (clans, contracts, flowers, goldfish) is what people did with a quarter-ton of rock. Part 2’s job is to make that sentence expensive. Not a caption. Hours. Heat. A princess who can see. A smith who has not yet agreed to look.</p>
      <p>The Mikaboshi were sorcerer kings the Soga drove off the mainland more than a thousand years ago. They survived under the sea in a habitat of branches, bodies adapted to Datenseki, and came back when the vein showed. Ariu’s insects, poisoned air, and hardened flesh are the royal kit. After chapter 119, a camp of explainers said Magatsumi is those insects recast in Kunishige’s steel. The camp is useful. It is not yet a caption this essay will print as fact. What is fact: once Magatsumi entered the field, Japan could walk onto the island. What is fact: after a treaty, Akemura used Malediction anyway. About 200,000 civilians. The Kamunabi filed it as victory. The war over a vein ended as a myth about heroes. Part 2 is the invoice before the filing.</p>

      <h2>Talks are a battlefield</h2>
      <p>Chapters 117 through 121 are titled as talks, not battles. That is the book’s joke and its thesis. A princess with foresight is a strategic weapon. A bureau that wants Datenseki without admitting it needs a picky civilian smith is a strategic coward. Hasumi’s lab fails. Shiba already knows whose eyes to hire. Mashiro does not want to steal ore for a weapons dealer. Giyu might trade Chiaki. Hiroto can crush a man with gravity and still die to a prince who grew up inside the mineral. The Enchanted Blades have not been forged. The war is already happening as a meeting. Jump’s English readers who wanted another hotel fight got a conference table. The table is the point. Malediction is what you get when the conference is later declared insufficient by the man who held the strongest sword.</p>
      <p>Kunishige, in this past, is not the hermit over a cellar. He is a man who will not sell to people he cannot stand, which means he barely eats. Subaru will like him because both of them are smiths who kept a civilian craft (sushi, pickiness) next to a lethal one. Enten’s goldfish are still years away. The household language of the seventh blade is being assembled as relationships, not as a design document. Chiaki is hope. Shiba is the friend who will tell him not to close his eyes in the fire. Akemura is not yet the uncle in the basement. He is the brother a princess loves. Part 1 taught you to hate the Sword Master. Part 2 is making you watch the country build him.</p>

      <h2>Smelting as ethics</h2>
      <p>Chapters 125 through 129 refuse montage. Smelting, Fire, Smelting, Smelting, Ironworks. Hokazono talked to a real swordsmith. The process is dangerous enough that Kunishige nearly dies in the shop in chapter 129, and the thing that pulls him back is not patriotism. It is Chiaki. The mineral wants to pop the user. The eyes are the only stabilizer. Sojo will later try to fake those eyes with Kyonagi flesh and will pop himself. Tenri will try a half-stable stone to impress Kyora and will pop himself. The present-tense plot is full of people dying of the lesson Part 2 is currently teaching in real time: Datenseki without Kunishige is a crater. Datenseki with Kunishige is a war crime with a warranty.</p>
      <p>True Realm, in the present, is the wielder’s brief locking with steel. In the past, the brief is still being written by a government. Kill the enemy. Protect the mainland. Make the vein usable. Those are not Chihiro’s brief. Chihiro’s brief, once he learns it, is fewer blades. Enten exists because this smelting succeeded too well. If you love Part 2’s craft and skip the Malediction essay, you are reading Sojo’s book: the work without the household. If you love the flowers essay and skip the smelting, you are reading the Kamunabi’s press release: the crime without the kiln. The vein requires both desks.</p>

      <h2>Atlantis was always the clock</h2>
      <p>Chapter 113’s color page (the island English Twitter called Japan’s Atlantis) is not Part 2’s first image. It is Part 1 admitting the clock. Shokoku rose about twenty-two years before the present. The war ends eighteen years before. Enten is forged about fifteen years after the war. The raid is three years before page one. The numbers were always a mineral’s biography. Part 2 finally puts a princess and a kiln on the same timeline instead of a revenge teen and a stolen katana. The YouTube desk will keep arguing cour 1 endings and paternity. This essay is for the quieter claim: the series was never only about who holds the swords. It was about who was willing to turn a quarter-ton of island into a personality, and who was sorry afterward, and who was not.</p>
      <p>When chapter 130 prints, the ironworks may finish a blade. This page will not guess which of the six comes first. Magatsumi is the sixth forged in some tallies and the strongest in all of them. Cloud Gouger is weather. Tobimune is support. Kumeyuri is fifth. The catalog will wait. Official chapters: VIZ / MANGA Plus. Related: <a href="../manga/part-2.html">Part 2 magazine desk</a>, <a href="../world/datenseki.html">Datenseki</a>, <a href="malediction.html">Malediction</a>, <a href="../characters/chiaki.html">Chiaki</a>.</p>
      <p class="related"><a href="../manga/part-2.html">Part 2</a><a href="malediction.html">Malediction</a><a href="../world/datenseki.html">Datenseki</a><a href="../arcs/seitei-war.html">Seitei War</a></p>
    </article>
    """,
)

